  "body": "**Independent verification; no \u03ba claim.** This PR re-checks [#2435](https://github.com/CrocSwap/integer-mult-bounds/pull/2435) (Jeremy Kothe, head `324d7d35`, conditional \u03ba = 0.0016985113437, the newest top T74 claim) with code written independently of #2435. The checkers are this author's earlier #2387 `fill_check80.py` and #2315 `words_check.py`, used unchanged as libraries.\n\n**Everything checked reproduces:**\n- **Words.** Both words, recounted by two implementations, match the reported profile {1:2359, 2:632, 3:330, 4:120, 5:38, 8:8} and inventory {4:33, 5:9, 7:62, 8:90, 9:240}, with 434 helpers and 78 zero buffers.\n  - All 46 warps pass: G invertible, K_G symplectic, Fourier rank 0.\n  - The exact replay over \u211a\u27e8F\u27e9 passes forward and dual with all 658 inputs dirty: Y += X, with everything else and all 78 buffers restored.\n- **Owner map.** `OWNERS.json.gz` (289,044 roles) passes rules R-a to R-g.\n  - The 1,332 windows were rebuilt from 2,220 GLOBAL-TEMPLATE events and match #2435's PLAN.\n  - X2 pending axes are disjoint, and the 9,129 distinct 73-column charts match SPEC `actual_73column_sigmas`.\n- **Recount equals #2435's SPEC, PROFILE and body.**\n  - Idle multiset `{1:20824, 3:6695, 5:1, 48:25302}`, global profile, 276,407 cross-replica roles, and rank mass 4,816,512 with deficit 23,680.\n  - Physical stock: 66,748 under #2322's in-tableau rule, plus 78 buffers charged separately, gives 66,826.\n- **Endpoint.** The root of the recounted profile is within \u00b11e-15 of the claimed \u03ba (800-bit enclosures). The claimed \u03ba also matches #2435's pinned `outer/OUTER-CLAIM.json`.\n- **Controls.** 16 owner-map and word negative controls plus a flipped-coefficient replay control are all rejected.\n\n**Structural finding: #2435's change is frame-only.** Its words differ from #2322's only in frames: 24 `start_extra` entrances, 24 A-gate frames and 48 B-gate frames per word. Registers, coefficients, warps, centres, ends and cleanup are byte-identical, and the script checks this.\n- The scalar identity is therefore #2322's, unchanged.\n- The one obligation specific to #2435 is that the parent hosting delivers those 24 copy buffers at a two-dimensional entrance frame. That is **not** checked here; #2435 covers it with its native tooling.\n\n**Related.** #2442 shows this fill is not the pattern-integer optimum for these words. The optimum would add up to +5.8e-10 if realizable. That does not affect the correctness verified here.\n\n**Review.** An adversarial AI reviewer ran about 20 additional mutations; every illegal one was rejected. It found the frame-only diff and three wording and hygiene issues: scope wording, a missing FAIL line on replay rejects, and an unpinned outer \u03ba. All are fixed.\n\n**Checks.** `--check-only`, the 3.10 grammar check and the research tests pass. Run on CPython 3.14.4; the registered 3.12 replay was not run.\n\n```sh\npython3 -I -B research/t74-2435-fill-independent-check/check_2435.py --fetch   # ~20 s\n# PASS_T74_2435_FILL_INDEPENDENT roles=289044 idle={\"1\":20824,\"3\":6695,\"48\":25302,\"5\":1} physical=66826 charts=9129 controls=16 root=kappa_2435+-1e-15\n```\n\n**Scope.**\n- Not checked: native lowering, invoice, precision tapes, outer ledger, bit supplier and admission. \u03ba = C \u2212 1/F \u2212 B is not re-derived.\n- Base: main `0fdd7d82`. Card: `independent-moment`, scope refined; the assignment is the independent-verification track, seed 83.\n\n**Credits.**\n- #2435 / #2374 / #2349 (Jeremy Kothe) and #2363 (mason-hale).\n- #2322 (Vlado Vojdanovski).\n- #2269 (Jeremy Kothe).\n- #2226 (Cinna Davis).\n- #2309 (Dugongue).\n- #2387 / #2315 (this author): the vendored checkers, pinned.\n\nPrepared with substantial AI assistance (Claude Code, Anthropic, Claude Opus 5.5). No independent human review is claimed. Apache-2.0.\n\n\ud83e\udd16 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
